# defaults-shared.config — `M154g` step 4a: `C93`'s positive half (`config:directive:defaults`).
#
# One `allow hosts` line in `defaults` and two envs whose base URLs both sit outside it. `TF036`
# fires for **whichever env is active**, which is the sharing claim stated as a diagnostic: the
# line was written once and is being read twice. Its control is `defaults-per-env.config`, which
# differs from this file by which block that line sits in and by nothing else.
#
# `example.test` rather than a real host because the whole leg is a `tflw check` — nothing resolves
# and nothing connects, and an RFC 6761 reserved name says so out loud.

defaults
  allow hosts "example.test"

env one default
  api "http://localhost:4001/v1"

env two
  api "http://127.0.0.1:4001/v1"
